text:
Lofty mountain, where Rome’s devastation
will forever proclaim your memory;
proud buildings where the glory
of great Carthage still shines;

deserted shore, once a peaceful lake,
filled with triumphs and victories;
shattered marbles, a history
that shows us what the world repays;

arches, amphitheaters, baths, temple,
celebrated buildings that you were,
whose traces we now scarcely see;

your example is a great remedy for my pain:
if time brought you down,
time can bring down my sorrows.
